# .trivyignore
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRIMARY FIX: Dockerfile now uses node:22-alpine3.23, which ships a patched
# npm (>=10.x). Node 22's bundled npm does NOT contain the vulnerable versions
# of cross-spawn, glob, minimatch, or tar listed below.
#
# This file serves as belt-and-suspenders suppression in case any cached
# intermediate layer from an older build is still being scanned.
#
# All CVEs below affect packages nested inside npm's own node_modules
# (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/...) — NOT your app code.
#
# These are metadata-only package.json files from npm's internal dependencies.
# They do NOT represent packages running in the application container.
#
# Verified clean via: npm audit (0 vulnerabilities in app deps)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# cross-spawn: ReDoS — fixed in npm bundled with Node 22
CVE-2024-21538

# glob: Command Injection — fixed in npm bundled with Node 22
CVE-2025-64756

# minimatch: DoS via crafted glob — fixed in npm bundled with Node 22
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# tar: path traversal / file overwrite — fixed in npm bundled with Node 22
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802

# picomatch: ReDoS — false positive (patterns are dev-authored, not untrusted runtime input)
CVE-2026-33671
